            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "i think i'm confused by the PR title \"preserve environment variables\".\n\nIIUC, the idea here is that `$` and `~` are literal chars in the path, _not_ environment variables. they just happen to \"look like\" env vars.\n\nbut still, in that case, it seems like `expand_env` makes more sense; we still want to normalize, because \"normalize\" by definition does not (should not) change the path (but \"expand\" does).",
            "commit_id": "1594ca23682b38bec161685f0c3a6f6548c3c337",
            "created_at": "2026-07-26T10:18:56Z",
